cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Adjacent-Layer Functional Specialization in Q2_K Quantized
  Gemma 4 31B: A Single-Question Pilot of L25 (Compute) and
  L26 (Meta-Verify)
message: >-
  If you use this software or patch in your research,
  please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Akito
    family-names: Hirai
    email: morphicode.jp@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0161-3249'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/morphicode-jp/f32-patch-gemma'
url: 'https://huggingface.co/morphicode-jp/gemma-4-31B-it-L25L26x1.5-Q2_K'
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20362821
    description: Zenodo archive of paper, code, and reproduction artifacts
abstract: >-
  We report a single-question pilot observation that scaling
  individual layer_output_scale tensors at layers 25 and 26 of
  Gemma 4 31B-it (Q2_K quantization) produces distinct behavioral
  phenotypes: L25-alone yields compute-confident answers with
  minimal mid-stream verification, L26-alone produces
  verification-dense but functional answers, and the joint scaling
  (paper v1 patch, L25+L26 multiplied by 1.5, 8 bytes total) produces
  explicit terminal-verification reflexes absent in either
  single-layer condition. The n=32 follow-up (exp166) statistically
  confirms an asymmetric auxiliary-explanation rate (L26-alone 56%
  vs L25-alone 16%, p<0.01) while finding accuracy differences not
  significant at n=32. This is a hypothesis-generating release; the
  asymmetry framing is provisional pending fuller replication. The
  paper v1 (L25+L26 mix, 8 bytes) GGUFs at Q1 (IQ1_M), Q2 (Q2_K),
  and Q4 (Q4_K_M) are distributed; per-layer ablation GGUFs
  (L25-alone, L26-alone, triple) are reproducible from the included
  bake scripts.
keywords:
  - LLM
  - quantization
  - gemma-4
  - per-layer-ablation
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - hypothesis-generating-pilot
